 "format": "ocd-check-bundle.v1",
 "limits": {
  "device_records": "For VoLTE, Wi-Fi calling, video calling and VoNR, a profile's value is a summary over every source and every phone model's table, made by the family rule above. It is not a vote or a count over phone models. generated/devices/carrier-variants.json holds the device records: what one phone model's own carrier file sets for the SIM, every device value OCD publishes, including those that agree with the profile value. A device record is configuration from one vendor or ROM file, not confirmed by a second source and not a test result. It holds for one software stack (stock firmware, a LineageOS tree, or Sony's AOSP tree), says nothing about the operator's offer or emergency calls, and is not an export: never write an off from it into a phone's settings. A phone model without a record for a profile and switch has no file OCD reads that sets a value there, or its value is older than five years, or its codename or model does not bind to one catalog device. It never means off, and it never means the device agrees with the profile value. docs/data-model.md describes the file.",
  "gates": "A carrier can still block a feature that its settings turn on. The usual gates are a list of approved phone models (common in the US, Australia and Sweden), an option you must book in your plan (LIDL Connect's Wi-Fi calling, for example), a carrier server that must approve the phone first (in the US, often with a registered emergency address for Wi-Fi calling), a service the operator has ended (MMS in Germany), roaming limits, and the Wi-Fi network you use (its DNS or firewall can keep Wi-Fi calling from reaching the carrier). None of these shows in carrier settings, so no source tells OCD about them; only a test with your SIM, plan and phone does. Some keys hint at a gate: carrier_volte_provisioning_required_bool and the REG09 Wi-Fi calling error mapping.",
  "missing_switch": "A switch that carrier-config-list.xml leaves out is not neutral: your phone keeps what its ROM already says, which for VoLTE, Wi-Fi calling and video calling is usually off, and for MMS, SMS over IMS and conference calls usually on.",
  "mvno_merge": "An MVNO without its own SPN, GID, or IMSI prefix in any source merges into the host network's profile. LIDL Connect runs on Vodafone Germany, and no profile names it, so its SIM resolves the 26202 profiles.",
  "not_verified": "No profile has been verified on a phone. Every value comes from a maintained source, not from a test call. No value has been tested for emergency calls; docs/consume.md says which keys a ROM should keep.",
  "readme_section": "Limits to read before you ship",
  "tables_not_tests": "A capability value says what carrier tables configure, not what works. It does not say the operator still offers the service: tables often keep a service for months or years after an operator ends it.",
  "value_meanings": {
   "conditional": "the sources disagree, often between phone models. Often one phone model's own table turns it off while others turn it on; generated/devices/carrier-variants.json shows which.",
   "supported": "at least one phone maker's or OS settings for this SIM turn the feature on, and no source whose off counts turns it off. It does not tell you that the carrier still offers it, that your plan includes it, or that your phone model is allowed.",
   "unknown": "no reliable source. It does not mean \"no\".",
   "unsupported": "the carrier's own settings, or two independent sources, turn it off."
  }
 },
